  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1220 PM EST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nIt is still quite cool today, and the stubborn clouds over our \nnortheast counties will eventually erode later today into this \nevening. The mostly clear sky for much of the night along with light \nwinds will allow overnight temperatures to dip to near or below \nfreezing across the entire area. \n\nThe upper trough that is currently edging off the east coast will \ncontinue to retreat, and our weather for the coming week will be \ndominated by surface high pressure and an upper ridge that builds in \nfrom the west. We will see dry weather along with a warming trend. \nAfter a cool start to the week, we will see temperatures around 5 to \n10 degrees above normal for the latter part of the week.  \n\nThere are some model solutions that show rain coming back into our \narea next weekend.  However, given the very poor model agreement/run \nto run consistency and the usual long range timing uncertainties, \nthe ensemble approach of the NBM which keeps us mainly dry through \nSunday looks reasonable.",
